  "description": "There is an invisible engine that ignites the spirit of every cyclist regardless of their ability. Something impalpable, a subconscious yearning that leads the cyclist to set off through nature amid climbs and descents without any kind of opponent or stopwatch to beat. What drives this engine is not the enjoyment of a challenge, but the desire to understand more about ourselves. About where we come from and where we want to go.\n\nThe new technical perspective of the Karga is underpinned by this vision and these values. The history and philosophy of Wilier are linked to the competition world. The experience accrued with the Wilier-Pirelli team has helped us grow in off-road riding. That invisible engine that spurs every cyclist has ignited our desire to break the mould. We went beyond the paradigm of lightweight e-MTB.\n\nWe discovered that Wilier’s racing DNA also looks great on a bike that doesn’t focus on competitions. That’s how we came up with the Karga.",
